[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Unit and Integration Testing in React Native: Jest and RNTL"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Testing is an essential part of building robust React Native applications. By combining Jest as the test runner and assertion library with React Native Testing Library (RNTL), you can verify both the individual units of your code and how your components interact with user actions."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"1. Installation and Setup"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Modern React Native projects configured with Expo or the CLI usually come with Jest pre-configured. If you need to install RNTL manually, run the following command in your terminal:"},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"npm install --save-dev @testing-library/react-native @testing-library/jest-native"},{"order":6,"type":"paragraph","text":"Ensure that your Jest configuration in package.json or jest.config.js includes the correct setup files for React Native Testing Library."},{"order":7,"type":"subheading","text":"2. Writing a Unit Test with Jest"},{"order":8,"type":"paragraph","text":"Unit tests focus on individual functions, custom hooks, or utility helpers without rendering UI components. Here is an example of testing a simple currency formatter utility."},{"order":9,"type":"code","text":"const formatCurrency = (amount) => {
  if (typeof amount !== 'number') return '$0.00';
  return `$${amount.toFixed(2)}`;
};

describe('formatCurrency', () => {
  it('formats numbers correctly', () => {
    expect(formatCurrency(10)).toBe('$10.00');
  });

  it('handles invalid inputs gracefully', () => {
    expect(formatCurrency('invalid')).toBe('$0.00');
  });
});"},{"order":10,"type":"subheading","text":"3. Writing an Integration Test with RNTL"},{"order":11,"type":"paragraph","text":"Integration tests ensure that multiple units work together. In React Native, this usually means rendering a component, simulating user input, and asserting the output or state change. Below is an example of a login form component."},{"order":12,"type":"code","text":"import React, { useState } from 'react';
import { View, TextInput, Button, Text } from 'react-native';

export const LoginForm = ({ onSubmit }) => {
  const [username, setUsername] = useState('');

  return (
    <View>
      <TextInput
        placeholder="Username"
        value={username}
        onChangeText={setUsername}
        testID="username-input"
      />
      <Button
        title="Submit"
        onPress={() => onSubmit(username)}
        testID="submit-btn"
      />
    </View>
  );
};"},{"order":13,"type":"paragraph","text":"Now, let us write the RNTL integration test to verify that typing into the input and pressing the button invokes our mock callback with the correct data."},{"order":14,"type":"code","text":"import React from 'react';
import { render, fireEvent } from '@testing-library/react-native';
import { LoginForm } from './LoginForm';

test('calls onSubmit with the entered username', () => {
  const handleSubmit = jest.fn();
  const { getByTestId } = render(<LoginForm onSubmit={handleSubmit} />);

  const input = getByTestId('username-input');
  const button = getByTestId('submit-btn');

  fireEvent.changeText(input, 'johndoe');
  fireEvent.press(button);

  expect(handleSubmit).toHaveBeenCalledWith('johndoe');
});"},{"order":15,"type":"subheading","text":"Best Practices for React Native Testing"},{"order":16,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Query by accessibility roles and text labels (e.g., getByRole, getByText) rather than testID whenever possible, as this encourages accessible UI design."},{"order":17,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Mock native modules and external libraries (like React Navigation or AsyncStorage) inside the jest.config.js or via setupFiles."},{"order":18,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Keep your tests focused on user behavior rather than internal component implementation details."}]
